\f1\b VT062617gfp_24C07chrim
\f0\b0 : VT062617 > GFP, 24C07 > Chrimson\
	-
\f1\b VT062617gfp_36B06chrim
\f0\b0 : VT062617 > GFP, 36B06 > Chrimson\
	-
\f1\b VT062617gfp_65C03chrim
\f0\b0 : VT062617 > GFP, 65C03 > crimson\
	-
\f1\b VT062617gfp_65C03chrim_VT062617tnte
\f0\b0 : VT062617 > GFP, VT062617 > TNTe, 65C03 > Chrimson\
	-
\f1\b VT062617gfp_FB5Vsplitchrim
\f0\b0 : VT062617 > GFP, VT013602AD; 78H12DBD > Chrimson\
	-
\f1\b VT062617gfp_FB6Msplitchrim
\f0\b0 : VT062617 > GFP, 49B08AD; VT063626DBD > Chrimson\
	-
\f1\b VT062617gfp_PFGsplitchrim
\f0\b0 : VT062617 > GFP, VT017491AD; VT000355DBD > Chrimson\
	-
\f1\b VT062617gfp_current
\f0\b0 : VT062617 > GFP (Chrimson expressed in various presynaptic cells)\
\
 Each of these structures have a single row for each cell, and contain the following fields:\
	-
\f1\b name
\f0\b0 : date and experiment number\
	-
\f1\b folder
\f0\b0 : pathname to folder containing raw data on local computer\
	-
\f1\b data
\f0\b0 : name of matlab structure containing metadata (found in raw data folder)\
	-
\f1\b N_ctrl
\f0\b0 : trial numbers for pre-drug data\
	-
\f1\b N_IMI
\f0\b0 : trial numbers for trials in the presence of imidacloprid (100 nM)\
	-
\f1\b N_curare
\f0\b0 : trial numbers for trials in the presence of curare (10 \'b5M)\
	-
\f1\b N_IMI_curare
\f0\b0 : trial numbers for trials in the presence of imidacloprid (100 nM) and curare (10 \'b5M)\
	-
\f1\b N_picro
\f0\b0 : trial numbers for trials in the presence of picrotoxin (5 \'b5M)\
	-
\f1\b N_picro_IMI_curare
\f0\b0 : trial numbers for trials in the presence of picrotoxin (5 \'b5M), imidacloprid (100 nM), and curare (10 \'b5M)\
	-
\f1\b N_methysergide
\f0\b0 : trial numbers for trials in the presence of methysergide (50 \'b5M)\
	-
\f1\b N_methysergide_IMI_curare
\f0\b0 : trial numbers for trials in the presence of methysergide (50 \'b5M), imidacloprid (100 nM), and curare (10 \'b5M)\
	-
\f1\b N_yohimbine
\f0\b0 : trial numbers for trials in the presence of yohimbine (10 \'b5M)\
	-
\f1\b voltage
\f0\b0 : matrix containing raw voltage values for each trial (samples X trial)\
	-
\f1\b current
\f0\b0 : matrix containing raw current values for each trial (samples X trial)\
	-
\f1\b stim_struct
\f0\b0 : data structure containing the trial numbers for each stimulus type (field #1 = stimulus type, field #2 = trial numbers)\
	-
\f1\b opto
\f0\b0 :  matrix containing optogenetic signal for each trial (samples X trial)\
	-
\f1\b wind
\f0\b0 : matrix containing binarized wind signal for each trial (samples X trial)\
	-
\f1\b odor
\f0\b0 : matrix containing binarized odor signal for each trial (samples X trial)\
	-
\f1\b sampratein
\f0\b0 : digitizer sample rate (10 kHz)\
	-
\f1\b samprateout
\f0\b0 : sample rate of stimulus (opto, wind, or odor signal) \
\
All data analyses in the manuscript are performed on these data structures. To see the code for creating the data structures, please see the code repository on GitHub (https://github.com/nagellab/Lanzetal2025)\
